  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/0d0a34d12bdf2318475e973d0151a0d6cb18c691949a209b11d3e725bdf58aa5.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin\u2061x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-sin\u2061x.$\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $3$ to give $y=-3sin\u2061x$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-3sin\u2061x.$",
